## 4. Available Agent Platforms at DBS Finance

DBS Finance currently has access to three platforms for building agent-like workflows, with two additional surfaces arriving in the near future. Each has a different capability profile, and choosing the right one matters.

### 4.1 DBS GPT (Workflow Builder)

DBS GPT is the internal AI platform available to all DBS staff. Its workflow builder allows users to chain prompts, add conditional logic, and build repeatable processes through a no-code UI.

**Strengths:**
- Accessible to non-technical users
- Approved and available within DBS's security perimeter
- Good for structured, linear workflows involving text generation and summarisation
- Familiar interface similar to ChatGPT

**Limitations:**
- Limited tool integration — it is difficult to connect to external APIs or internal data systems
- The underlying model is not best-in-class for complex reasoning tasks
- Workflow logic is linear; genuine agent loops and dynamic decision-making are not well supported
- Not well suited for tasks requiring high reasoning quality or nuanced financial analysis

**Best used for:** Drafting, summarisation, document processing, simple multi-step text workflows where reasoning depth is not the bottleneck.

### 4.2 Microsoft Copilot Studio

Copilot Studio is Microsoft's platform for building AI-powered workflows and bots, integrated with the Microsoft 365 ecosystem.

**Strengths:**
- Strong native integration with Microsoft products — Teams, SharePoint, Excel, Outlook
- Better for workflows that live inside the Microsoft ecosystem (e.g. a Teams bot that answers questions from a SharePoint knowledge base)
- No-code/low-code builder with reasonable flexibility
- Supports connectors to a range of enterprise systems

**Limitations:**
- Reasoning quality is moderate; complex financial logic or nuanced analysis will hit limits
- Agent loop capability is limited — it is better thought of as a workflow engine with AI bolted on
- Integration outside the Microsoft stack requires additional configuration effort
- Cost and licensing considerations within DBS's enterprise agreement

**Best used for:** Microsoft-native workflows — e.g. a Copilot that answers Finance policy questions from a SharePoint repository, or a Teams bot that triggers a report generation process. Strong fit when the primary integration surface is M365.

### 4.3 Claude Code *(Coming Soon)*

Claude Code is Anthropic's agentic coding tool, operated via the command line. It is designed for developers and technical users who want an AI that can autonomously read, write, and execute code within a project.

**Strengths:**
- Significantly higher reasoning and coding quality than DBS GPT or Copilot Studio
- True agent behaviour — it can explore a codebase, plan a solution, write and run code, check outputs, and iterate
- Strong fit for technical Finance workflows: building data pipelines, automating reconciliation scripts, developing and testing new tools
- Can integrate with MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers to connect to internal systems and APIs
- Operates in the developer's local environment with full auditability of actions taken

**Limitations:**
- Requires technical users — this is not a no-code tool
- Command-line interface; not suitable for end-user-facing deployments
- Governance for agentic code execution in a regulated environment needs to be defined (see Section 8)
- Still arriving at DBS; availability timeline to be confirmed

**Best used for:** Developer-led automation, building and iterating on Finance tools and scripts, technical prototyping of agent workflows before broader deployment.

### 4.4 Claude Cowork *(Coming Soon)*

Claude Cowork is a desktop application designed for non-developers to automate file and task management using AI. It brings agentic capability to knowledge workers without requiring coding skills.

**Strengths:**
- True agent behaviour accessible to non-technical Finance staff
- Can operate on files, folders, and desktop workflows autonomously
- Higher reasoning quality than DBS GPT or Copilot Studio
- Designed for knowledge worker productivity tasks — a natural fit for Finance analysts and operations staff

**Limitations:**
- Desktop application; deployment and IT approval process at DBS to be confirmed
- Still arriving; capability details subject to change
- As with any agentic tool, requires clear guardrails on what the agent is permitted to do autonomously

**Best used for:** Finance staff who need genuine agent capability without writing code — e.g. automating document processing, file organisation, report preparation workflows.

