## 5. Platform Selection Guide

Use the following framework to choose the right platform for your use case.

| Criterion | DBS GPT | Copilot Studio | Claude Code | Claude Cowork |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| User type | All staff | All staff | Developers | All staff |
| Reasoning quality | Moderate | Moderate | High | High |
| True agent loops | Limited | Limited | Yes | Yes |
| Tool / API integration | Limited | M365-native | Extensive (MCP) | Moderate |
| No-code UI | Yes | Yes | No | Yes |
| Available now | Yes | Yes | Soon | Soon |
| Best fit | Simple text workflows | M365-integrated workflows | Technical automation | Knowledge worker automation |

**Decision rules in plain language:**

- If the task is text-based and straightforward → **DBS GPT**
- If the task lives inside Microsoft 365 and needs Teams/SharePoint integration → **Copilot Studio**
- If you are a developer building or automating a technical Finance process → **Claude Code** (when available)
- If you are a Finance analyst who needs genuine agent capability without coding → **Claude Cowork** (when available)
- If the task requires high reasoning quality and true multi-step agent behaviour today → escalate to the Finance AI team to discuss interim options

When in doubt, default to the simpler tool. Agents introduce risk and complexity. If DBS GPT or a structured Copilot Studio workflow can get 80% of the way there, that is often the right answer for now.

